Subject: [GTK] Do not use accelerated compositing when GL is a software rasterizer

Draft against the webkitgtk-2.52.6 release tarball. Apply with -p1 from the
tarball root. Independent of the other drafts (applies with an offset of one
line after 0004). Compiled and measured (dev/bench/RESULTS.md).

What it does
  In the UI process, where WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE is resolved
  (HardwareAccelerationManager), hardware acceleration is now also considered
  unavailable when the EGL display GTK uses is backed by a software device:
  the EGL device advertises EGL_MESA_device_software, or its renderer string
  (EGL_EXT_device_query_name) contains llvmpipe, softpipe or swrast. The
  result is the same as WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE=1: preferences start
  with accelerated compositing off (WebPreferencesGtk.cpp), no
  AcceleratedBackingStore is created, and pages are painted with Skia on the
  CPU through the UpdateInfo path, dirty rects only.

  WEBKIT_FORCE_COMPOSITING_MODE set to anything but 0 keeps compositing on a
  software rasterizer. That variable already exists in 2.52 (its only other
  meaning is "0 = do not force").

How to check it took effect
  webkit_settings_get_hardware_acceleration_policy() returns NEVER, and
  webkit://gpu shows the hardware acceleration policy as "never".

What it does not handle
  - No glGetString(GL_RENDERER) fallback (2.54's GLDisplay::isSoftwareRendered
    has one): there is no current GL context at this point. A software driver
    that exposes neither EGL extension is not detected.
  - webkit_settings_set_hardware_acceleration_policy(ALWAYS) cannot turn
    compositing back on in that case (it returns early when hardware
    acceleration is unavailable); only the environment variable can.
  - Everything that depends on accelerated compositing is lost on software
    GL: async scrolling, 3D transforms, compositor driven animations.
  - 2.54 needs a different patch: there the same test belongs in
    HardwareAccelerationManager and must also clear hardware acceleration,
    since WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE alone keeps GL painting.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
@@ -144,6 +144,41 @@
     return false;
 }
 
+#ifndef EGL_RENDERER_EXT
+#define EGL_RENDERER_EXT 0x335F
+#endif
+
+bool AcceleratedBackingStore::isSoftwareRendered()
+{
+    static bool isSoftwareRendered;
+    static std::once_flag onceFlag;
+    std::call_once(onceFlag, [] {
+        auto* glDisplay = Display::singleton().glDisplay();
+        if (!glDisplay)
+            return;
+
+        if (!GLContext::isExtensionSupported(eglQueryString(nullptr, EGL_EXTENSIONS), "EGL_EXT_device_query"))
+            return;
+
+        EGLDeviceEXT device = nullptr;
+        if (!eglQueryDisplayAttribEXT(glDisplay->eglDisplay(), EGL_DEVICE_EXT, reinterpret_cast<EGLAttrib*>(&device)) || !device)
+            return;
+
+        const char* deviceExtensions = eglQueryDeviceStringEXT(device, EGL_EXTENSIONS);
+        if (GLContext::isExtensionSupported(deviceExtensions, "EGL_MESA_device_software")) {
+            isSoftwareRendered = true;
+            return;
+        }
+
+        if (!GLContext::isExtensionSupported(deviceExtensions, "EGL_EXT_device_query_name"))
+            return;
+
+        if (const char* renderer = eglQueryDeviceStringEXT(device, EGL_RENDERER_EXT))
+            isSoftwareRendered = g_strrstr(renderer, "llvmpipe") || g_strrstr(renderer, "softpipe") || g_strrstr(renderer, "swrast");
+    });
+    return isSoftwareRendered;
+}
+
 #if USE(GBM)
 Vector<RendererBufferFormat> AcceleratedBackingStore::preferredBufferFormats()
 {
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/AcceleratedBackingStore.h
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/AcceleratedBackingStore.h
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@
 
     static OptionSet<RendererBufferTransportMode> rendererBufferTransportMode();
     static bool checkRequirements();
+    static bool isSoftwareRendered();
 #if USE(GBM)
     static Vector<RendererBufferFormat> preferredBufferFormats();
 #endif
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/HardwareAccelerationManager.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/gtk/HardwareAccelerationManager.cpp
@@ -42,15 +42,23 @@
     : m_canUseHardwareAcceleration(true)
     , m_forceHardwareAcceleration(true)
 {
+    const char* forceCompositing = getenv("WEBKIT_FORCE_COMPOSITING_MODE");
+
 #if !ENABLE(WEBGL)
     m_canUseHardwareAcceleration = false;
 #else
     const char* disableCompositing = getenv("WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE");
     if ((disableCompositing && strcmp(disableCompositing, "0")) || !AcceleratedBackingStore::checkRequirements())
         m_canUseHardwareAcceleration = false;
+
+    // A software rasterizer composites and reads back the whole view on the CPU for every frame, which
+    // costs more than painting the dirty rects without GL. WEBKIT_FORCE_COMPOSITING_MODE set to anything
+    // but 0 keeps accelerated compositing.
+    bool isCompositingForced = forceCompositing && strcmp(forceCompositing, "0");
+    if (m_canUseHardwareAcceleration && !isCompositingForced && AcceleratedBackingStore::isSoftwareRendered())
+        m_canUseHardwareAcceleration = false;
 #endif
 
-    const char* forceCompositing = getenv("WEBKIT_FORCE_COMPOSITING_MODE");
     if (forceCompositing && !strcmp(forceCompositing, "0"))
         m_forceHardwareAcceleration = false;
 }
